  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1223 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe only item of note is a threat for shallow fog overnight into\ntomorrow morning near Lake Michigan where a modestly more moist\nenvironment will advect inland. Otherwise, no significant \nweather is expected the next 7 days with above to much above \naverage temperatures each day. Generally light winds should \nallow weak lake breezes to form each of the next several \nafternoons, but probably only result in slightly cooler \nconditions right near the lake. Other than a bit of mid-high \nlevel cloudiness this afternoon, much of the week looks to be \nmostly sunny.\n\n- Izzi/Borchardt",
